sndk='''# V6.0 SNDK causal reconstruction — what should have been visible before the surge\n\n## Claim boundary\n\nThis is a timestamped causal reconstruction and acquisition blueprint, not a completed SNDK backtest. The bundled equity panel ends before the 2025–2026 episode and contains no fresh point-in-time analyst, borrow, NAND contract-price or customer-qualification history. Live weight remains zero.\n\n## Observable chain\n\n1. **14 August 2025 baseline expectation:** Sandisk guided fiscal Q1 revenue to $2.10–$2.20 billion.\n2. **6 November 2025 expectation break:** reported $2.31 billion, 21% sequential growth and above guidance; Datacenter grew 26%. Management disclosed two hyperscalers in qualification plus a third hyperscaler and a top storage OEM planned for calendar 2026.\n3. **29 January 2026 persistence:** Q2 revenue reached $3.03 billion, 31% sequential growth; Datacenter grew 64%, linked to AI infrastructure builders and deployments at scale.\n4. **30 April 2026 value-capture confirmation:** Q3 revenue reached $5.95 billion, 97% sequential growth; Datacenter grew 233%, pricing rose, and Q4 guidance moved to $7.75–$8.25 billion. The 10-Q attributed the expansion to both ASP per gigabyte and exabytes sold.\n\n## What the early detector must measure\n\n- analyst revenue/EPS revision velocity and breadth;\n- guidance-versus-consensus gap;\n- NAND contract and spot pricing, inventory and capacity utilization;\n- hyperscaler qualification stage and conversion to volume orders;\n- datacenter exabyte shipment and ASP inflection;\n- gross-margin sensitivity to ASP versus cost per gigabyte;\n- customer mix and new business-model agreements;\n- supplier/customer read-through;\n- short interest, borrow fee and option/flow only as vulnerability/transmission layers.\n\n## What probably did not originate the move\n\nTotal OI, realized liquidation, generic volume surge and technical momentum may have amplified or confirmed the repricing, but they do not explain why earnings power changed.\n\n## Frozen research target\n\nAt each historical filing/estimate date, predict whether a stock will enter the top-K future residual-return set while retaining at least 50% of the eventual move. Compare expectation/bottleneck features against price-volume, momentum, valuation and sector baselines; require validation, untouched lockbox, lead time, remaining return, MAE and prospective evidence.\n'''
(ROOT/'V60_SNDK_CAUSAL_RECONSTRUCTION.md').write_text(sndk)

report=f'''# War Room OS V6.0 — Deep Early-Move Driver Research\n\n## Bottom line\n\nOpen interest and long/short liquidation improve **attribution**, but do not by themselves solve early discovery. Total OI is symmetric; realized liquidation is usually a transmission event after the move begins. The research architecture is therefore frozen as:\n\n`origin → vulnerability → trigger → transmission/amplification → exhaustion`\n\n## Empirical work completed\n\n- Total empirical claim records accounted: **{total:,}**.\n- Price/volume extreme-move claims: **{pricevol:,}**, production survivors: **0**.\n- Historical maintained factor-pair claims: **{studies[-1]['claims']:,}**.\n- Historical full-gate factor pairs: **{studies[-1]['historical_full_gate']:,}**.\n- Strict post-discovery robustness survivors: **{studies[-1]['strict_robustness_survivors']}**.\n- Fresh point-in-time stock-level production drivers: **0**.\n\nThe 61 factor-pair robustness survivors are an acquisition priority, not a live signal. Frequent families include net payout/external financing, volatility/ownership interactions and a small cluster involving institutional ownership conditional on extreme short interest.\n\n## What changed after adding OI and liquidation logic\n\n1. `price up + OI up` is no longer labeled long accumulation. It is ambiguous new risk until signed flow or participant books resolve the side.\n2. New long building, new short building, short covering and long liquidation are separate states.\n3. Side-specific liquidations are normalized to depth/ADV and classified as move-underway amplification.\n4. Early cascade risk uses OI/leverage relative to depth, funding, basis, crowding and liquidation distance **before** forced orders print.\n5. Fundamental/physical/expectation/broker/on-chain origin layers remain separate so the system can answer what actually started the move.\n\n## Negative result that matters\n\nBrute-forcing more public OHLCV formulas is not the path to SNDK-like early discovery. Across {pricevol:,} massive-move price/volume claims, nothing passed the production gates. This falsifies the current data-ready implementations; it does not prove that every technical feature in existence is useless.\n\n## Highest-value next evidence panels\n\n- **US stocks:** point-in-time analyst revisions, filings/guidance, customer qualification, industry pricing/capacity, borrow fee/utilization, signed options/equity flow.\n- **IHSG:** historical ticker-broker inventory, crossings, foreign flow, free float/controller and done detail.\n- **Commodities:** COT/TFF plus inventory surprises, curve, physical basis, freight/storage and signed hedging flow.\n- **FX:** rate-path surprise, TFF, funding basis, options risk reversal and intervention/reserve state.\n- **Crypto:** multi-venue OI, funding, basis, taker flow, depth, liquidation distance/prints, spot/on-chain/stablecoin origin.\n\n## Harness status\n\nThe derivatives test harness passes planted-signal, null and timing controls. It detects a planted origin/vulnerability signal, produces zero null survivors and does not promote realized liquidation as an early driver. This validates the harness, **not** a market edge.\n\n## Governance\n\n- Live predictive weight: `0.0`.\n- Capital permission: `BLOCKED`.\n- No ticker is relabeled proven.\n- Every missing licensed/point-in-time panel fails closed.\n- No unrestricted formula mining after outcomes.\n'''
(ROOT/'V60_DEEP_DRIVER_RESEARCH_FINAL.md').write_text(report)
status=f'''# War Room OS V6.0 — Final Status\n\n`RESEARCH_ARCHITECTURE_AND_DATA_READY_BATTERIES_PASS / PRODUCTION_EARLY_MOVE_EDGE_NOT_YET_PROVEN / CAPITAL_BLOCKED`\n\n## Completed\n\n- Exact V5.8 → V5.9 ancestry preserved.\n- Cross-market mechanical-flow attribution added.\n- Total OI explicitly non-directional.\n- Long/short liquidation, covering, new positioning and deleveraging separated.\n- Origin/vulnerability/trigger/transmission state model frozen.\n- 193 mechanism primitives and {json.loads((R/'V60_CAUSAL_PATH_REGISTRY.json').read_text())['path_count']:,} mechanistic paths registered.\n- {total:,} empirical claim records globally accounted.\n- {pricevol:,} price/volume extreme-move claims completed with zero production survivor.\n- 89,464 factor-pair historical tests completed; 61 survive extra robustness but remain non-point-in-time research candidates.\n- Derivatives synthetic planted/null/timing controls pass.\n\n## Not honestly completed\n\n- Fresh point-in-time SNDK-like winner reconstruction.\n- Licensed borrow, signed options, physical basis, historical IHSG broker inventory and complete multi-venue crypto liquidation panels.\n- Untouched cross-market lockbox and prospective profitability.\n\n## Release policy\n\nPredictive components promoted: **0**  \nLive research weight: **0.0**  \nCapital permission: **BLOCKED**\n'''
